"settings.mcp.guideSteps" = "1. Upgrade the self-hosted Worker and apply the database migration.\n2. Turn on sharing and use the buttons above to copy the service address and read-only token.\n3. Add a remote MCP in a client that supports Streamable HTTP: you can paste the copied client config directly; for manual setup, enter the /mcp address and set the Authorization header to Bearer <read-only token>.\n4. After connecting you should see quota_list, quota_get, and quota_health; run quota_health to check observability first, then query quotas.\n5. Tokens expire after 90 days; turning off sharing or rotating the token revokes access. MCP cannot trigger collection — the Mac needs to keep updating.";
